{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-039",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 39,
  "title": "Job 39",
  "display_title": "Job 39",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 39,
  "sortOrder": 18039,
  "verseCount": 30,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Knowest thou the time when the wild goats of the rock bring forth? or canst thou mark when the hinds do calve?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Canst thou number the months that they fulfil? or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "They bow themselves, they bring forth their young ones, they cast out their sorrows.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Their young ones are in good liking, they grow up with corn; they go forth, and return not unto them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Who hath sent out the wild ass free? or who hath loosed the bands of the wild ass?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Whose house I have made the wilderness, and the barren land his dwellings.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "He scorneth the multitude of the city, neither regardeth he the crying of the driver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The range of the mountains is his pasture, and he searcheth after every green thing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Will the unicorn be willing to serve thee, or abide by thy crib?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Canst thou bind the unicorn with his band in the furrow? or will he harrow the valleys after thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Wilt thou trust him, because his strength is great? or wilt thou leave thy labour to him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Wilt thou believe him, that he will bring home thy seed, and gather it into thy barn?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Gavest thou the goodly wings unto the peacocks? or wings and feathers unto the ostrich?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Which leaveth her eggs in the earth, and warmeth them in dust,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And forgetteth that the foot may crush them, or that the wild beast may break them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "She is hardened against her young ones, as though they were not hers: her labour is in vain without fear;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Because God hath deprived her of wisdom, neither hath he imparted to her understanding.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "What time she lifteth up herself on high, she scorneth the horse and his rider.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Hast thou given the horse strength? hast thou clothed his neck with thunder?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Canst thou make him afraid as a grasshopper? the glory of his nostrils is terrible.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "He paweth in the valley, and rejoiceth in his strength: he goeth on to meet the armed men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He mocketh at fear, and is not affrighted; neither turneth he back from the sword.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The quiver rattleth against him, the glittering spear and the shield.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage: neither believeth he that it is the sound of the trumpet.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha; and he smelleth the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom, and stretch her wings toward the south?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Doth the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest on high?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "She dwelleth and abideth on the rock, upon the crag of the rock, and the strong place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "From thence she seeketh the prey, and her eyes behold afar off.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:39:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Her young ones also suck up blood: and where the slain are, there is she.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 39:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:39:30"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
